# Linksets: per-resource metadata (LWS 1.0 core section 9.1, RFC 9264).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: "LWS 1.0 core: linksets"
comment: >-
  A resource's metadata lives in a linkset resource that a client finds only through
  rel="linkset"; no path convention is one a client may assume, so every test here
  follows the relation the server advertises. Section 9.1 then fixes how the linkset
  is served, advertised, edited and retired.
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/
entries:

  - id: "#getLinkset"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: getLinkset
    label: The linkset a resource advertises is served as application/linkset+json with an ETag
    comment: >-
      lws-test-suite's version fetched /alice/notes/.meta directly; .meta appears in the
      draft only in examples. Here the linkset of a data resource and of a container are
      each reached through their rel="linkset" link, and each is a linkset document.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Get, Linkset, DataResource, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-standalone-rfc9264
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-media-type-json
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#getLinkset
    supersedes: [core/linkset-discovery-and-patch-advertisement]
    steps:
      - label: create a data resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${test.container}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource with metadata
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: created
      - label: reading it names its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the linkset is served as a linkset document with an entity tag
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/linkset+json
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: ETag
              present: true
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset
              jsonType: array
      - label: the test container names its linkset too
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: containerLinkset
      - label: and that linkset is served the same way
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${containerLinkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/linkset+json
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset
              jsonType: array

  - id: "#linkset-advertises-patch"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: linkset-advertises-patch
    label: A linkset advertises GET and PATCH in Allow and JSON Merge Patch in Accept-Patch
    comment: >-
      A client that cannot learn whether a linkset takes PATCH, or in which format, has
      to guess and handle the 405 or 415 it gets wrong. Both headers are MUSTs.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Get, Linkset]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-allow-get-patch
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-accept-patch-advertised
    supersedes: [core/linkset-discovery-and-patch-advertisement]
    steps:
      - label: create a data resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${test.container}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource with metadata
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: created
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the linkset says how it may be edited
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Allow
              matches: '(?i)^(?=.*\bGET\b)(?=.*\bPATCH\b)'
            - headerName: Accept-Patch
              matches: '(?i)application/merge-patch\+json'

  - id: "#linkset-conditional-412"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: linkset-conditional-412
    label: A linkset PATCH with a failing precondition is refused with 412
    comment: >-
      "When a server receives a conditional request for which the precondition fails, it
      MUST reject the request with a 412 Precondition Failed status code."
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#update-resource
    traits: [Patch, Linkset, Conditional]
    note: >-
      Catalog entry linkset-if-match-412-428 carries the 21 August text (If-Match required,
      428 when absent); the 21 September draft keeps only the 412 MUST. Not cited until
      the catalog is re-baselined.
    steps:
      - label: create a data resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${test.container}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource with metadata
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: created
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: a PATCH carrying a validator that never matched is refused
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/merge-patch+json
          ifMatch: '"touchstone-stale-etag"'
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${created}"
                license:
                  - href: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
        response:
          statusCode: 412

  - id: "#linkset-put-405-when-unsupported"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: linkset-put-405-when-unsupported
    label: A linkset that does not advertise PUT refuses it with 405
    comment: >-
      PUT on a linkset is optional and advertised through Allow; "If the server does not
      support PUT, it MUST reject the request with 405 Method Not Allowed". A linkset
      whose Allow names PUT makes the test inapplicable.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Put, Linkset]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-put-405-if-unsupported
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-optional-methods-advertised
    steps:
      - label: create a data resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${test.container}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource with metadata
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: created
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the linkset does not advertise PUT (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Allow
              matches: '(?i)^(?!.*\bPUT\b)'
      - label: a PUT is refused with 405 and the methods that are allowed
        request:
          method: PUT
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/linkset+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${created}"
                license:
                  - href: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
        response:
          statusCode: 405
          otherHeaders:
            - headerName: Allow
              present: true

  - id: "#linkset-removed-with-resource"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: linkset-removed-with-resource
    label: Deleting a resource removes its linkset
    comment: >-
      "Deleting a resource MUST result in the automatic removal of its associated linkset
      resource metadata." A linkset outliving its resource would describe nothing.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#delete-resource
    traits: [Delete, Linkset, DataResource]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-lifecycle-tied-to-resource
    steps:
      - label: create a data resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${test.container}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource with metadata
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: created
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: the linkset exists
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
      - label: delete the resource
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${created}"
          ifMatch: current
        response:
          statusCode: 204
      - label: its linkset is gone with it
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: [404, 410]

  - id: "#linkset-patch-merge"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: linkset-patch-merge
    label: A JSON Merge Patch adds a user-managed link to a linkset
    comment: >-
      Servers "MUST support PATCH using application/merge-patch+json" on linksets, but a
      merge patch replaces the linkset array wholesale and servers "MAY restrict
      modifications to specific links", so whether a given patch is accepted depends on
      restrictions the draft leaves open. The happy path is therefore a SHOULD: patch in
      a license link and read it back.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20260921/#metadata
    traits: [Patch, Linkset]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/linkset-patch-merge-patch
    steps:
      - label: create a data resource
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${test.container}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a resource that will get a license
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: created
      - label: find its linkset
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          linkHeaders:
            - rel: linkset
              capture: linkset
      - label: merge-patch a license link into it
        request:
          method: PATCH
          url: "${linkset}"
          contentType: application/merge-patch+json
          ifMatch: current
          bodyJSON:
            linkset:
              - anchor: "${created}"
                license:
                  - href: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: the linkset now carries the license
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${linkset}"
          accept: application/linkset+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /linkset
              some:
                - pointer: /license
                  some:
                    - pointer: /href
                      equals: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
